Warning [jet.MapGroupRoundTrip]: `group` copies the whole group out of `groups` and stores it back
  --> tests/ui_lint/map_group_round_trip.jet:10:9
    |
 10 |         group := groups.get(p.dept) ?? [Person]{}
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `group` still shares the entry's buffer when it is written, so the write first copies the whole group, and storing it back drops the Map's old copy; in a loop that is quadratic. The build grows the entry in place only when the Map is a variable the function declares, the statements before the store neither name it nor `break` or `next`, and nothing after the store names the group
 Fix: Grow the entry in place: `if !groups.has_key(p.dept) -> groups[p.dept] = [Person]{}`, then `groups[p.dept].insert(…)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0534

Warning [jet.MapGroupRoundTrip]: `group` copies the whole group out of `names` and stores it back
  --> tests/ui_lint/map_group_round_trip.jet:68:9
    |
 68 |         group := names.get(p.dept) ?? []
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `group` still shares the entry's buffer when it is written, so the write first copies the whole group, and storing it back drops the Map's old copy; in a loop that is quadratic. The build grows the entry in place only when the Map is a variable the function declares, the statements before the store neither name it nor `break` or `next`, and nothing after the store names the group
 Fix: Grow the entry in place: `if !names.has_key(p.dept) -> names[p.dept] = []`, then `names[p.dept].push(…)`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0534
